hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"553","I went to Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) to ask for something, so Lady Aisha informed me: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say this in this house: ""O Allah! Whoever is made responsible for any affair of my Ummah and deals harshly with them, then be harsh with him, and whoever is made responsible for any affair of my Ummah and deals gently with them, then be gentle with him."
"554","from the Prophet ﷺ who said: Do not associate with anyone other than a believer not let anyone other than a God-fearing person eat from the meal ˹you serve.˺"
"555","The Prophet ﷺ said: Associate only with a believer, and let only a God-fearing man eat your meals. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4832)"
"556","Messenger of Allah! A man loves some people, but he cannot do work like their work. He replied; Yes, Abu Dharr, will be with those whom you love. Abu Dharr then repeated it. The Messenger of Allah (May peace be upon him) also repeated it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5126)"
"557","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A person will be with those whom he loves."
"558","I was in the company of Allah's Apostle ﷺ as he had been sitting in Ji'rana (a place) between Mecca and Medina and Bilal was also there, that there came to Allah's Apostle ﷺ a desert Arab, and he said: Muhammad, fulfill your promise that you made with me. Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: Accept glad tidings. Thereupon the desert Arab said: You shower glad tidings upon me very much; then Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned towards Abu Musa and Bilal seemingly in a state of annoyance and said: Verily he has rejected glad tidings but you two should accept them. We said: Messenger of Allah, we have readily accepted them. Then Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a cup of water and washed his hands in that and face too and put the saliva in it and then said: Drink out of it and pour it over your faces and over your chest and gladden yourselves. They took hold of the cup and did as Messenger of Allah ﷺ had commanded them to do. Thereupon Umm Salama called from behind the veil: Spare some water in your vessel for your mother also, and they also gave some water which had been spared for her. (Using translation from Muslim 2497)"
"559","that the Prophet ﷺ said, “There are blessings with your elders.”"
"560","The Prophet ﷺ said: Associate only with a believer, and let only a God-fearing man eat your meals. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4832)"
"561","The Prophet ﷺ said, 'The example of a good pious companion and an evil one is that of a person carrying musk and another blowing a pair of bellows. The one who is carrying musk will either give you some perfume as a present, or you will buy some from him, or you will get a good smell from him, but the one who is blowing a pair of bellows will either burn your clothes or you will get a bad smell from him."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 5534)"
"562","The Prophet (peace be upon him) gestured to him with his blessed hand to come forward. The man said: What is your opinion about a person who loves a people but is not able to join them? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: He will be with those whom he loves. The words of the narration ""Haum"" mean that this word was said in a voice louder than that of the Bedouin, so that the Bedouin would not be sinful for raising his voice above the voice of the Prophet (peace be upon him). This has been narrated from the Shaykh."
"563","When would be the Last Hour? Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: What preparation have you made for that? Thereupon he said: The love of Allah and of His Messenger (that is my preparation for the Last Hour) (for the Day of Resurrection). Thereupon he (the Holy Prophet) said: You would be along with one whom you love. (Using translation from Muslim 2639a)"
"564","I have not prepared many deeds for it, but I love Allah and His Messenger."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""You will be with those whom you love, and you will receive the reward you hope for."
"565","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""It will certainly come to pass, but what preparation have you made for it?"" He replied, ""I have not prepared much in terms of deeds, but I love Allah and His Messenger."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""You will be with those whom you love."" The narrator states: At that time, there was an Ansari man named Muhammad present with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""If he remains alive, the Hour will be established before he becomes old."" Here, the narrator named Hadbah has narrated these additional words. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We love Allah and His Messenger. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): This narration belongs to those in which the address is kept general, and by it is meant prohibition, that is, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to prohibit people from inclining towards this world, and he described before them the virtue of something related to their eternal life, the reality of which accepts that the time of the Hour is near for those people, and they should not rely on what they are hearing."
"566","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whenever two people love each other for the sake of Allah, then the better of the two is the one who has more intense love for his companion."
"567","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever deceives us is not from us; deceit and trickery will be in the Hellfire."
"568","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whoever deceives another person regarding his wife is not from among us, and whoever turns a woman against her husband is not from among us."
"569","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: Have you told him this? I replied: No. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Tell this to your brother. The narrator says: I went after that person. I caught up with him. I held him by the shoulder. I greeted him with salam and said: By Allah! I love you for the sake of Allah. He also said: By Allah! I also love you for the sake of Allah Almighty. I told him: If the Prophet of Allah had not commanded me to tell you this, I would not have done so. In narrating this tradition, the narrator named Azraq bin Ali is unique, and this has been stated by the Shaykh."
"570","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""When a person loves his brother, he should inform him."
"571","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, ""Have you told him this?"" He replied, ""No."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Get up and tell him."" So the man got up, went to him, and said, ""O so-and-so! By Allah, I love you."" The man replied, ""May He for whose sake you love me, love you in return."
"572","A person visited his brother in another town and Allah deputed an Angel to wait for him on his way and when he came to him he said: Where do you intend to go? He said: I intend to go to my brother in this town. He said: Have you done any favour to him (the repayment of which you intend to get)? He said: No, excepting this that I love Mm for the sake of Allah, the Exalted and Glorious. Thereupon he said: I am a meesenger to you from, Allah: (to inform you) that Allah loves you as you love him (for His sake). (Using translation from Muslim 2567a)"
"573","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, among the servants of Allah are some people who are not prophets, but the prophets and martyrs will envy them.” It was asked: Who are these people? (Tell us about them) so that we may love them. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: They are those who love one another for the sake of Allah’s pleasure, without any kinship or other worldly connection. Their faces will be full of light and they will be upon pulpits made of light. When people will be afraid, they will have no fear; when people will be sad, they will have no sadness. Then he recited this verse: “Behold! Indeed, the friends of Allah will have no fear, nor will they grieve.”"
"574","Verily. Allah would say on the Day of Resurrection: Where are those who have mutual love for My Glory's sake? Today I shall shelter them in My shadow when there is no other shadow but the shadow of Mine. (Using translation from Muslim 2566)"
"575","The next day I came early, and I saw that the young man had arrived before me. I found him performing prayer. Abu Adrees says: I kept waiting for him until he completed his prayer, then I approached him from the front. I greeted him with salam and said: By Allah! I love you for the sake of Allah. He asked: For the sake of Allah, is it? I replied: For the sake of Allah. He took hold of the edge of my cloak and pulled me towards himself and said: Receive this glad tidings! I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “Allah the Exalted says: My love is obligatory for those who love each other for My sake, who sit together for My sake, and who meet each other for My sake.” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Abu Adrees Khawlani’s name is ‘Aidhullah bin Abdullah. He was the leader of the experts in the science of recitation from Syria in his time. He is the one who refused to fight Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) on behalf of Sayyiduna Mu’awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him). When he said to Sayyiduna Mu’awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him): Who are you to fight Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) and dispute with him regarding the caliphate? You are not like him. You are not the husband of a lady like Sayyidah Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her). You are not the father of Sayyiduna Imam Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Imam Husain (may Allah be pleased with him). You are not the cousin of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Sayyiduna Mu’awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) feared that he might corrupt the minds of the reciters of Syria, so Sayyiduna Mu’awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: I am seeking retribution for the blood of Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him). He replied: Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) did not kill him. Sayyiduna Mu’awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: But he is preventing retribution from being taken from the killer of Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: Be patient, I will go to him and try to find out the reality. Then he came to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), greeted him with salam, and then said: Who killed Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him)? Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: Allah the Exalted killed him, and I am with him. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) meant: I too am among the slain with him. And according to one narration: He meant that Allah the Exalted intended for him to be killed, and I tried to avoid it. (But) Abu Adrees Khawlani could not understand the meaning of Sayyiduna Ali’s (may Allah be pleased with him) words, and he gathered a group from Syria and encouraged them (to fight against Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him)."
"576","A person visited his brother in another town and Allah deputed an Angel to wait for him on his way and when he came to him he said: Where do you intend to go? He said: I intend to go to my brother in this town. He said: Have you done any favour to him (the repayment of which you intend to get)? He said: No, excepting this that I love Mm for the sake of Allah, the Exalted and Glorious. Thereupon he said: I am a meesenger to you from, Allah: (to inform you) that Allah loves you as you love him (for His sake). (Using translation from Muslim 2567a)"
"577","The narrator says: He pulled the edge of my cloak and then said: If you are truthful, then receive this glad tidings. I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Those who love each other for the sake of Allah will be under the shade of the Throne on the Day when there will be no shade except His Throne, and the Prophets and martyrs will envy their status."" The narrator says: I left from there and went to Sayyiduna 'Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him). I narrated to him the hadith that Sayyiduna Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) had narrated, so Sayyiduna 'Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) narrate from his Lord: ""(Allah Almighty says:) My love has become obligatory for those who love each other for My sake. My love has become obligatory for those who show goodwill to each other for My sake. My love has become obligatory for those who visit each other for My sake. My love has become obligatory for those who spend on each other for My sake. These people will be on pulpits of light, and the Prophets and the truthful will envy their status."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Abu Muslim Khawlani is Abdullah bin Thawb. He is Yamani and a Tabi'i. He is among the virtuous and best of the Tabi'in. He is the one to whom 'Ansi said: Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? He replied: No. He ('Ansi) asked: Do you testify that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah? He replied: Yes. By the order of 'Ansi, a large fire was lit, and he was threatened that he would be thrown into it if he did not support him in his claim, but he did not accept it. So he ('Ansi) threw him into the fire, but the fire did not harm him. 'Ansi considered this a great matter. By his order, he was sent to Yemen. He was expelled from there, so he came to Madinah Munawwarah, where he met Sayyiduna 'Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him). He asked him: Where have you come from? He informed him about this. Sayyiduna 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: What happened to that young man who was burned? He replied: He was not burned. Sayyiduna 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) realized that he was the one. Sayyiduna 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I ask you by Allah's name, are you Abu Muslim? He replied: Yes. So Sayyiduna 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) took his hand and brought him to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and narrated the whole incident to him, and both of them were very happy about it. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""All praise is due to Allah, who has shown us in this Ummah a person who was burned like Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him), but was not burned."" It is also narrated: His wife was very beautiful. One of his neighbors tried to corrupt this woman, so he supplicated against her: O Allah! Whoever wants to corrupt my wife, make her blind. That woman was sitting with her husband eating dinner. During this, she asked: Have you put out the lamp? Her husband replied: No. She said: I have become blind. I cannot see anything. Then she was informed about the supplication of Abu Muslim against her, so she came to him and said: I tried to do such and such regarding your wife. I also deceived her. Now I repent. Please supplicate to Allah Almighty to return my sight. He prayed to Allah and said: O Allah! Return the sight of this woman, so Allah Almighty returned her sight."
"578","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: In Hell. When he turned to leave, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him back and said: My father and your father are in Hell."
"579","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of a good companion is like that of a perfume seller; even if you do not buy anything from him, his fragrance will still reach you. And the example of a bad companion is like that of a blacksmith; even if he does not burn you with his sparks, his foul smell will still reach you."
"580","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade two to converse (privately) to the exclusion of a third."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3776)"
"581","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) has said: 'Two people should not converse secretly with each other leaving out the third.'"
"582","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) were present near a house in the market of Khalid bin Utbah. There a man came and wanted to speak in secret with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both). At that time, besides me and that man, there was no one else with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) who wanted to speak with him in secret. So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) called another person, until we became four people. Then he said to me and to the person whom he had called: ""You both move aside."" I heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Two people should not converse secretly excluding a third."
"583","""When you are three, two should not converse (privately) to the exclusion of their companion, because that makes him sad."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3775)"
"584","I asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): What if there are four people? He replied: Then there is no harm to you."
"585","The Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""There are three types of gatherings. (That is, three kinds of people participate in a gathering): One who is safe (that is, the one who remains silent), one who gains benefit (that is, the one who enjoins good), and one who is regretful (the one who speaks wrongly)."
"586","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade that a person should make another stand up from his place and then sit there himself. Rather, you should make room and accommodate each other."
"587","None of you should make another one stand in the meeting and then occupy his place. (Using translation from Muslim 2177a)"
"588","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person gets up from a gathering and then returns to it, he has more right to his place."
"589","I came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and I saw him sitting while reclining on a cushion that was on his left side."
"590","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When some people gather in an assembly, and then disperse from that assembly without remembering Allah and without sending blessings upon the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), then this will be a cause of regret for them on the Day of Resurrection."
"591","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whenever some people gather at a place and do not remember Allah there, nor do they send blessings upon the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), then this will be a cause of regret for them on the Day of Resurrection, even if they are admitted into Paradise for reward."
"592","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever some people sit together in a place and do not remember Allah there, nor do they send blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), then this will be a cause of regret for them on the Day of Resurrection, even if those people enter Paradise."
"593","There are some expressions which a man utters three times when he gets up from an assembly he will be forgiven for what happened in the assembly; and no one utters them in an assembly held for a noble cause or for remembrance of Allah but that is stamped with them just as a document is stamped with a signet-ring. These expressions are: Glory be to Thee, O Allah, and I begin with praise of Thee, there is no god but thou; I ask Thy pardon, and return to Thee in repentance. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4857)"
"594","I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance,' then whatever mistakes he made in that gathering will be forgiven."
"595","Avoid sitting on the paths. They (his Companions) said: Messenger of Allah, there is no other help to it (but to sit there as we) hold our meetings and discuss matters there. Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: If you have to sit at all, then fulfil the rights, of the path. They said: What are their rights? Thereupon he said: Keeping the eye downward (so that you may not stare at the women), refraining from doing some harm to the other and exchanging mutual greetings (saying as-Salamu 'Alaikum to one another) and commanding the good and forbidding the evil. (Using translation from Muslim 2121a)"
"596","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade sitting on the thresholds of houses. The people said: O Messenger of Allah! We are not able to avoid it and we do not have the strength (i.e., we are compelled to do so). The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If that is the case, then fulfill its rights. The people asked: What are its rights, O Messenger of Allah? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Responding to greetings, replying to one who sneezes and praises Allah, lowering the gaze, and guiding the way."
"597","narrates: Once the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) passed by a gathering of the Ansar and said: “If you insist on sitting, then guide those on the way, respond to greetings, and help those in need.”"
"598","that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Indeed Allah loves sneezing and He dislikes the yawn. So when one of you sneezes and says 'Al-Hamdulillah (All praise is due to Allah),' then it is a right due from every one who hears him to say: 'Yarhamukallah (May Allah have mercy upon you)' As for yawning then when one of you yawns let him suppress it as much as possible and not say: ""Hah Hah' for that is only from Ash-Shaitan laughing at him."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2747)"
"599","I participated in a battle with Salim bin Ubaid. Among those present, a man sneezed and said: ""As-salamu alaikum."" So Salim said: ""Peace be upon you and upon your mother as well."" This man disliked it very much. Salim said to him: ""Perhaps you disliked this."" He replied: ""I do not like that my mother be mentioned, whether with good or with bad."" So Salim said: ""We were on a journey with the Prophet (peace be upon him). A man sneezed and said: 'As-salamu alaikum.' So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: 'Peace be upon you and upon your mother as well?' When a person sneezes, he should say: 'Alhamdulillah ala kulli hal' or 'Alhamdulillah Rabbil Alameen,' and the other person should reply with: 'Yarhamukallah,' and he should say in response: 'Yaghfirullahu lakum' (May Allah forgive you)."
"600","The Prophet replied to the sneeze of one of them and did not reply to the other. He said: This person praised Allah, and this person did not praise Allah."
"601","Two men sneezed in the presence of the prophet (May peace be upon him). He said : Allah have mercy on you! To one and not to the other. He was asked: Messenger of Allah! Two persons sneezed. Ahmad’s version has: You invoked a blessing on one of them and left the other. He replied : This man praised Allah, and this man did not praise Allah. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5039)"
"602","I sneezed, but you did not respond to me. This man sneezed, and you responded to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: He mentioned Allah, so I mentioned him, and you forgot, so I also forgot you."
"603","when a man sneezed beside the prophet (May peace be upon him), he said to him : Allah have mercy on you, but when he sneezed again, he said : The man has a cold in the head. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5037)"
"604","""Shall I not tell you of the best of the people in status?"" We said: ""Yes. O Messenger of Allah!"" He said: ""A man who rides his horse in the cause of Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, until he dies or is killed. Shall I not tell you of the one who comes after him (in status)?"" We said: ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah!"" He said; ""A man who withdraws to a mountain pass and establishes Salah, and pays Zakah, and keeps away from the evil of people. Shall I not tell you of the worst of people?"" We said: ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah!"" He said: ""The one who asks for the sake of Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, but does not give (when he is asked) for His sake,"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2569)"
"605","That the Prophet ﷺ said: ""Shall I not inform you of the best of the people ? A man who takes hold of the reins of his horse in Allah's cause. Shall I not inform you of the one who comes after him ? The man who secludes himself from the people with a small group of sheep of his, thereby fulfilling Allah's right. Shall I not inform you about the worst of the people ? A man who is asked by (the Name of) Allah, but not given by Him."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1652)"
"606","“Which of the people is best?” He said: “A man who strives in Jihad in the cause of Allah with himself and his wealth.” He said: “Then who?” He said: “A man in a mountain pass who worships Allah and leaves the people from his evil.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3978)"
"607","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the words that people have found from the first Prophethood (i.e., the previous noble Prophets) is this: 'If you feel no shame, then do whatever you wish.'"" The narrator named Qanabi heard only this hadith from Shu'bah; this has been stated by the Sheikh."
"608","“Modesty is part of faith, and faith will be in Paradise. Obscenity in speech is part of harshness and harshness will be in Hell.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4184)"
"609","“Modesty is part of faith, and faith will be in Paradise. Obscenity in speech is part of harshness and harshness will be in Hell.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4184)"
"610","The Messenger of Allah [SAW] passed by a man who was censuring his brother about modesty. He said: ""Let him be, for modesty is part of faith."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5033)"
"611","There was a person before you who had killed ninety-nine persons and then made an inquiry about the learned persons of the world (who could show him the way to salvation). He was directed to a monk. He came to him and told him that he had killed ninety-nine persons and asked him whether there was any scope for his repentance to be accepted. He said: No. He killed him also and thus completed one hundred. He then asked about the learned persons of the earth and he was directed to a scholar, and he told him that he had killed one hundred persons and asked him whether there was any scope for his repentance to be accepted. He said: Yes; what stands between you and the repentance? You better go to such and such land; there are people devoted to prayer and worship and you also worship along with them and do not come to the land of yours since it was an evil land (for you). So he went away and he had hardly covered half the distance when death came to him and there was a dispute between the angels of mercy and the angels of punishment. The angels of mercy said: This man has come as a penitant and remorseful to Allah and the angels of punishment said: He has done no good at all. Then there came another angel in the form of a human being in order to decide between them. He said: You measure the land to which he has drawn near. They measured it and found him nearer to the land where he intended to go (the land of piety), and so the angels of mercy took possession of it. Qatada said that Hasan told him that it was said to them that as death approached him, he crawled upon his chest (and managed) to slip in the land of mercy. (Using translation from Muslim 2766a)"
"612","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him: He was asked: Have you heard the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, say this: Remorse is repentance? He replied: Yes."
"613","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): Did the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say this statement? ""Remors"
"614","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \""Remorse is repentance.\"""""""
"615","The monk replied: No. So that man killed the monk as well. Then he kept inquiring, and a person said to him: Go to such-and-such town. Then death came to that man and he passed away. There was a dispute between the angels of mercy and the angels of punishment regarding him. So Allah Almighty revealed to this (part of) the land to come closer, and to the other part to move farther away. Thus, the man was found to be a handspan closer to that (part, i.e., where he was going), so he was forgiven."
"616","The example of a believer and faith is like that of a horse tied to its peg; it wanders around but then returns to the same place. When a believer strays, he then returns to faith. O people! Feed your food to the pious and direct your good deeds towards the people of faith."
"617","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Allah Almighty is more pleased with the repentance of His servant than that person who, upon waking up, finds his camel which he had lost in a barren, waterless land."
"618","""Allah is more pleased with the repentance of one of you that a man in a desolate, barren, destructive wasteland, who has his mount carrying his provisions, his food, and his drink and what he needs with him. Then it wanders away. So he goes to find it until he is on the brink of death. He says: 'I will return to the place where I lost it, to die.' So he returns to his place and his eyes become heavy (falling asleep). Then he awakens to find his mount at his head carrying his food, drink and what he needs."" Other chains report similar narrations. (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2498)"
"619","I have made oppression unlawful for Myself and I have made it unlawful among you as well, so do not oppress one another. O My servants! Indeed, you commit sins by day and by night, and I am the One who forgives sins, and I do not mind."" After this, the narrator mentioned a lengthy hadith, at the end of which he stated this point. Whenever the narrator named Abu Idris would narrate this hadith, he would kneel down on his knees."
"620","The narrator says: Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) became silent, then she said: Once, the Prophet (peace be upon him) said at night: O Aisha! Allow me so that I may worship my Lord tonight. I said: By Allah! I love your company and I also love what pleases you. Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) stood up, performed ablution well, then stood up and began to offer voluntary prayers. Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) began to weep, until the hollow of his eye became wet. Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Then he wept and continued to weep until his beard became wet. Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Then he continued to weep, and wept for so long that the ground became wet. Then Bilal came and called him for the (Fajr) prayer. When he saw him weeping, he said: O Messenger of Allah! Why are you weeping, when Allah Almighty has forgiven your past and future (sins)? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Should I not be a grateful servant? Tonight a verse has been revealed to me. Woe to the one who recites it and does not ponder over it. (That verse is:) ""Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth..."" This is the complete verse."",""She fell silent for a while and then said"",""""""One night"","" he said"","" 'O Aisha"","" let me worship my Lord tonight.' I said"","" 'By Allah"","" I love your nearness"","" and I love what makes you happy.' She said"","" 'So he got up"","" purified himself"","" and stood to pray. He continued weeping until his lap became wet. Then he wept"","" and he did not stop weeping until his beard became wet. Then he wept"","" and he did not stop weeping until the ground became wet. Bilal came to announce the prayer to him"","" and when he saw him weeping"","" he said"","" 'O Messenger of Allah"","" why do you weep when Allah has forgiven all your past and future sins?' He said"","" 'Shall I not be a grateful servant? Tonight a verse has been revealed to me"","" woe to one who recites it and does not reflect on it: {Indeed"","" in the creation of the heavens and the earth} [and what follows] the entire verse.'"""""""""
"621","The people mentioned happiness in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), then they mentioned a lost thing which a person finds. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah is more pleased with the repentance of any one of you than a person who finds his lost thing in a barren land."
"622","The narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words:) I have done a deed, so forgive me. Allah Almighty said: My servant has committed a sin, he knows that he has a Lord who can forgive sins and can also punish for them, so I have forgiven My servant. Then that person committed another sin. (The narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words:) He committed another sin, so he said: O my Lord! I have committed a sin, so forgive me. Allah Almighty said: This My servant knows that he has a Lord who can forgive sins and can also punish for them, so I have forgiven My servant. Then that person again committed that sin. (The narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words:) He committed some other sin, then he said: O my Lord! I have committed a sin, so forgive me. Allah Almighty said: My servant knows that he has a Lord who can forgive sins and can also punish for them. O angels! I make you witnesses that I have forgiven My servant, now let him do whatever he wishes.”"
"623","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever commits a sin, then performs ablution and offers two units of prayer, and then seeks forgiveness from Allah the Exalted for that sin, Allah the Exalted grants him forgiveness."
"624","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to her: O Aisha! If you intended to commit a sin, then seek forgiveness from Allah and repent, because when a servant commits a sin and then seeks forgiveness from Allah, Allah forgives him. Wail has mentioned only three narrations on the authority of his son. This has been stated by the Sheikh."
"625","The words of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): “Do whatever you wish.” These are words of warning, behind which is a promise. And by the Prophet’s (peace and blessings be upon him) statement: “Do whatever you wish,” what is meant is: Do not disobey. And by the Prophet’s (peace and blessings be upon him) words: “I have forgiven you,” what is meant is, when you repent."
"626","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is that a person dies in such a state that he is a polytheist."
"627","The people asked: ""O Messenger of Allah! What is meant by the occurrence of the barrier?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That a person dies in such a state that he is a polytheist."
"628","“Allah accepts the repentance of His slave so long as the death rattle has not yet reached his throat.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4253)"
"629","He who seeks repentance (from the Lord) before the rising of the sun from the west (before the Day of Resurrection), Allah turns to him with Mercy. (Using translation from Muslim 2703)"
"630","No Muslim would die but Allah would admit in his stead a Jew or a Christian in Hell-Fire. 'Umar b. Abd al-'Aziz took an oath: By One besides Whom there is no god but He, thrice that his father had narrated that to him from Messenger of Allah ﷺ. (Using translation from Muslim 2767b)"
"631","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): “Having good expectations about Allah is a part of good worship.”"
"632","I did not expect this. Allah Almighty will ask: What did you expect? He will say: I expected that when You have taken me out of it (Hell), You would not return me to it again. So Allah Almighty will have mercy on that person and will admit him into Paradise."
"633","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) say: “Allah Almighty says: I am as My servant thinks of Me. Now it is up to him to think of Me as he wishes.”"
"634","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) quoting the statement of Allah, the Exalted: “I am as My servant thinks of Me. So let him think of Me as he wishes.”"
"635","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) quoting the statement of Allah, the Exalted: Allah, the Exalted, says, “I am as My servant thinks of Me. So let him think of Me as he wishes.”"
"636","I heard Allah's Apostle ﷺ as saying three days before his death: None of you should court death but only hoping good from Allah (Using translation from Muslim 2877a)"
"637","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say three days before his passing: ""Whoever among you is able, at the time of death, to have good expectations from Allah Almighty, then he should do so."
"638","I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say three days before his death: No one of you dies but he had good faith in Allah. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3113)"
"639","The narrator named Abu Yunus is Salim bin Jubair, and he is a Tabi'i."
"640","from the Prophet ﷺ narrating from his Lord ﷻ who said, ""By My Might, I neither combine two fears within My servant nor two securities. If he is fearful of Me in this world, I secure him on the Day of Judgement, and if he feels secure from Me in this world, I instill fear in him on the Day of Judgement."
"641","Sayyiduna Wathilah bin Asqa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) who was also going to visit him. We reached Yazid, and when he saw Sayyiduna Wathilah (may Allah be pleased with him), he stretched out his hand and began to gesture towards him. Sayyiduna Wathilah (may Allah be pleased with him) moved forward and sat down, so Yazid took hold of both the hands of Sayyiduna Wathilah (may Allah be pleased with him) and placed them on his own face. Sayyiduna Wathilah (may Allah be pleased with him) asked him: What is your opinion about Allah the Exalted? Yazid replied: By Allah! My opinion about Allah the Exalted is good. So Sayyiduna Wathilah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Then accept glad tidings, for I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Allah the Exalted says: I am as My servant thinks of Me. Whether he thinks good or bad.”"
"642","Abdullah b. Qais reported from Messenger of Allah ﷺ that none is more forbearing in listening to the most irksome things than Allah, the Exalted. They associate rivals with him, attribute sonhood to Him, but in spite of this He provides them sustenance, grants them safety, confers upon them so many things. (Using translation from Muslim 2804c)"
"643","narrator named Abu Nasr heard this narration from Kharijah bin Zaid, from his father."
"644","I am warning you about Hell, I am warning you about Hell, I am warning you about Hell.” (Sayyiduna Nu’man, may Allah be pleased with him, states) If the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) were in my place—Sayyiduna Nu’man (may Allah be pleased with him) was in Kufa at that time—even the people of the market would have heard this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), to the extent that the cloak on his shoulder fell down to his feet."
"645","The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, a man will take his father's hand and will want to take him into Paradise, but it will be called out: Beware! No polytheist will enter Paradise. Then that person will say: O my Lord! This is my father. The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Then his father will be made extremely ugly and foul-smelling, so that person will leave him."" Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id, may Allah be pleased with him, says: People used to say: This refers to the matter of Sayyiduna Ibrahim, peace be upon him (and his father), however, the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, did not say anything further about this."
"646","The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said the same to the descendants of Abd Manaf. He said the same to the descendants of Abdul Muttalib. Then he said: O Fatimah, daughter of Muhammad! Save yourself from the Fire, for I do not possess any power to harm or benefit you, except that I have kinship with you. I will benefit you with that. Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says: This narration is abrogated, because in it, it is mentioned that no person will intercede for another, but (the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him) was later granted the right of intercession in Madinah Munawwarah."
"647","I do not declare lawful for them any corruption in that which You have declared righteous. By Allah! These people will fall upside down regarding the religion of my Ummah just as a vessel is turned upside down in the field.”"
"648","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who is the most pious."" The people said, ""We are not asking you about this."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then are you asking about the chiefs of the Arabs? Those among you who were considered the best in the pre-Islamic period will also be considered the best in Islam, provided they gain understanding (of religious teachings)."
"649","I been to you?' They replied: 'You were the best father.' He said: 'By Allah! I have not stored any good deeds for the court of Allah Almighty, so now my Lord will punish me. So when I die, burn me, then crush me, and scatter me in a fast-blowing wind.' Allah Almighty said: 'Stand up.' So the man stood up. Allah Almighty asked: 'Why did you do this?' He replied: 'Out of fear of You.'” The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul, Allah Almighty forgave him."
"650","I to you? They replied: You were the best father. The man said: When I die, burn me, then crush me, and when a strong wind is blowing, scatter me. The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: That man died, and it was done to him as he had asked. Allah Almighty said to him: Be (as you were), and he stood up as a human even before the blink of an eye. Allah Almighty said: O My servant, why did you do this? He replied: O my Lord! Out of fear of You. The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Allah Almighty rewarded him by forgiving him."" The narrator named Mu'tamir states: My father narrated this to me. I related this narration to Abu 'Uthman Nahdi, and he said: Sulaiman narrated this hadith to me in the same way, but he added these words: ""You should throw me into the river."
"651","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""A grave-robber passed away. He said to his son: Burn me, then crush me and scatter me in the wind. He was asked: Why did you do this? He replied: O my Lord! Out of fear of You. So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah Almighty forgave him."
"652","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said regarding this verse: (The command of Allah, the Exalted, is) ""When the matter will be decided and those people will be in heedlessness."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: This is about the world."
"653","Behold, my Lord commanded me that I should teach you which you do not know and which He has taught me today. (He has instructed thus): The property which I have conferred upon them is lawful for them. I have created My servants as one having a natural inclination to the worship of Allah but it is Satan who turns them away from the right religion and he makes unlawful what has been declared lawful for them and he commands them to ascribe partnership with Me, although he has no justification for that. And verily, Allah looked towards the people of the world and He showed hatred for the Arabs and the non-Arabs, but with the exception of some remnants from the People of the Book. And He (further) said: I have sent thee (the Holy Prophet) in order to put you to test and put (those to test) through you. And I sent the Book to you which cannot be washed away by water, so that you may recite it while in the state of wakefulness or sleep. Verily, Allah commanded me to burn (kill) the Quraish. I said: My Lord, they would break my head (like the tearing) of bread, and Allah said: You turn them out as they turned you out, you fight against them and We shall help you in this, you should spend and you would be conferred upon. You send an army and I would send an army five times greater than that. Fight against those who disobey you along with those who obey you. The inmates of Paradise are three: One who wields authority and is just and fair, one who Is truthful and has been endowed with power to do good deeds. And the person who is merciful and kind hearted towards his relatives and to every pious Muslim, and one who does not stretch his hand in spite of having a large family to support. And He said: The inmates of Hell are five: the weak who lack power to (avoid evil), the (carefree) who pursue (everything irrespective of the fact that it is good or evil) and who do not have any care for their family or for their wealth. And those dishonest whose greed cannot be concealed even in the case of minor things. And the third. who betray you. morning and evening, in regard to your family and your property. He also made a mention of the miser and the liar and those who are in the habit of abusing people and using obscene and foul language. Abu Ghassan in his narration did not make mention of"" Spend and there would be spent for you."" (Using translation from Muslim 2865a)"
"654","I have created all My servants as Muslims, and whatever I have granted to My servants, it is lawful for them. The devils come to people and mislead them regarding their religion; they declare unlawful for them those things which I have declared lawful for them, and they command them to associate partners with Me, about which I have not sent down any command.” (The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, says:) “Before sending me as a Prophet, Allah Almighty turned His attention to the earth and expressed displeasure towards all the Arabs and all the non-Arabs, except for a few remnants among the People of the Book. Allah said to me: I have revealed a Book which water cannot wash away; recite it in both sleep and wakefulness. Allah commanded me to inform the Quraysh of this. I said: O my Lord! In that case, they will crush my head and grind it to dust. Allah Almighty said: Expel them as they expelled you, and fight them as they fought you, and spend (in My cause), We will spend on you, and send forth an army, We will send five like it, and whoever obeys you, fight alongside him against the one who disobeys you.”"
"655","Messenger of Allah ﷺ very often used to ask his companions, ""Did anyone of you see a dream?"" So dreams would be narrated to him by those whom Allah wished to tell. One morning the Prophet ﷺ said, ""Last night two persons came to me (in a dream) and woke me up and said to me, 'Proceed!' I set out with them and we came across a man lying down, and behold, another man was standing over his head, holding a big rock. Behold, he was throwing the rock at the man's head, injuring it. The rock rolled away and the thrower followed it and took it back. By the time he reached the man, his head returned to the normal state. The thrower then did the same as he had done before. I said to my two companions, 'Subhan Allah! Who are these two persons?' They said, 'Proceed!' So we proceeded and came to a man lying flat on his back and another man standing over his head with an iron hook, and behold, he would put the hook in one side of the man's mouth and tear off that side of his face to the back (of the neck) and similarly tear his nose from front to back and his eye from front to back. Then he turned to the other side of the man's face and did just as he had done with the other side. He hardly completed this side when the other side returned to its normal state. Then he returned to it to repeat what he had done before. I said to my two companions, 'Subhan Allah! Who are these two persons?' They said to me, 'Proceed!' So we proceeded and came across something like a Tannur (a kind of baking oven, a pit usually clay-lined for baking bread)."" I think the Prophet ﷺ said, ""In that oven there was much noise and voices."" The Prophet ﷺ added, ""We looked into it and found naked men and women, and behold, a flame of fire was reaching to them from underneath, and when it reached them, they cried loudly. I asked them, 'Who are these?' They said to me, 'Proceed!' And so we proceeded and came across a river."" I think he said, "".... red like blood."" The Prophet ﷺ added, ""And behold, in the river there was a man swimming, and on the bank there was a man who had collected many stones. Behold, while the other man was swimming, he went near him. The former opened his mouth and the latter (on the bank) threw a stone into his mouth whereupon he went swimming again. He returned and every time the performance was repeated. I asked my two companions, 'Who are these (two) persons?' They replied, 'Proceed! Proceed!' And we proceeded till we came to a man with a repulsive appearance, the most repulsive appearance, you ever saw a man having! Beside him there was a fire and he was kindling it and running around it. I asked my companions, 'Who is this (man)?' They said to me, 'Proceed! Proceed!' So we proceeded till we reached a garden of deep green dense vegetation, having all sorts of spring colors. In the midst of the garden there was a very tall man and I could hardly see his head because of his great height, and around him there were children in such a large number as I have never seen. I said to my companions, 'Who is this?' They replied, 'Proceed! Proceed!' So we proceeded till we came to a majestic huge garden, greater and better than I have ever seen! My two companions said to me, 'Go up' and I went up. The Prophet ﷺ added, ""So we ascended till we reached a city built of gold and silver bricks and we went to its gate and asked (the gatekeeper) to open the gate, and it was opened and we entered the city and found in it, men with one side of their bodies as handsome as the handsomest person you have ever seen, and the other side as ugly as the ugliest person you have ever seen. My two companions ordered those men to throw themselves into the river. Behold, there was a river flowing across (the city), and its water was like milk in whiteness. Those men went and threw themselves in it and then returned to us after the ugliness (of their bodies) had disappeared and they became in the best shape."" The Prophet ﷺ further added, ""My two companions (angels) said to me, 'This place is the Eden Paradise, and that is your place.' I raised up my sight, and behold, there I saw a palace like a white cloud! My two companions said to me, 'That (palace) is your place.' I said to them, 'May Allah bless you both! Let me enter it.' They replied, 'As for now, you will not enter it, but you shall enter it (one day). I said to them, 'I have seen many wonders tonight. What does all that mean which I have seen?' They replied, 'We will inform you: As for the first man you came upon whose head was being injured with the rock, he is the symbol of the one who studies the Qur'an and then neither recites it nor acts on its orders, and sleeps, neglecting the enjoined prayers. As for the man you came upon whose sides of mouth, nostrils and eyes were torn off from front to back, he is the symbol of the man who goes out of his house in the morning and tells so many lies that it spreads all over the world. And those naked men and women whom you saw in a construction resembling an oven, they are the adulterers and the adulteresses. And the man whom you saw swimming in the river and given a stone to swallow, is the eater of usury (Riba). And the bad looking man whom you saw near the fire kindling it and going round it, is Malik, the gatekeeper of Hell. And the tall man whom you saw in the garden, is Abraham and the children around him are those children who die with Al-Fitra (the Islamic Faith). The narrator added: Some Muslims asked the Prophet, ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! What about the children of pagans?"" The Prophet ﷺ replied, ""And also the children of pagans."" The Prophet ﷺ added, ""My two companions added, 'The men you saw half handsome and half ugly were those persons who had mixed an act that was good with another that was bad, but Allah forgave them.'"" (Using translation from Bukhārī 7047)"
"656","If a believer were to know the punishment (in Hell) none would have the audacity to aspire for Paradise (but he would earnestly desire to be rescued from Hell), and if a non-believer were to know what is there with Allah as a mercy. none would have been disappointed in regard to Paradise. (Using translation from Muslim 2755)"
"657","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If Allah were to call me and the son of Maryam to account for the shortcomings of these two (fingers) (the Prophet, peace be upon him, pointed to his thumb and the finger next to it), and He were to punish us, He would not be doing us any injustice."
"658","I fear that it might be a punishment that has been imposed upon my Ummah."
"659","The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""If Allah were to call me and ‘Isa (Jesus) to account for our sins and punish us, He would not be doing us any injustice."" The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, indicated this by gesturing with his index finger and the finger next to it."
"660","“Be moderate and adhere to moderation, for there is no one among you who will be saved by his deeds.” They said: “Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Not even me. Unless Allah encompasses me with mercy and grace from Him.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4201)"
"661","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Paradise is nearer to any of you than the Shirak (leather strap) of his shoe, and so is the (Hell) Fire. (Using translation from Bukhārī 6488)"
"662","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""If you knew that which I know, you would laugh little and weep much."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6486)"
"663","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him): ""A believer is not bitten from the same hole twice."" These words of the narration are from Umar bin Saeed Sinan."
"664","narrates: When a strong wind would blow, the effect of anxiety would be visible on the face of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). This was so that a person would not fall into self-conceit regarding this matter, even if that person was virtuous in himself and pious in his religion."
"665","I presented myself in the mosque before the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). At that time, he was standing and performing prayer, and a sound was coming from his chest like the sound of a boiling pot."
"666","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up and said: Strive to save yourselves from Hellfire. Then he turned his face away and trie"
